From: OpenWiFi BCM4360 Project <bcm4360@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] brcmfmac: pcie: BCM4360 INTERNAL_MEM reset NULL guard

The BCM4360 has no BCMA_CORE_INTERNAL_MEM core, so
brcmf_chip_get_core() returns NULL and upstream's unconditional
brcmf_chip_resetcore() dereferences it on the 4360 exit_download_state
path. Extend the existing BCM43602-only reset to also cover the
BCM4360 and guard the call with a NULL check (kimptoc
reference/brcmfmac-reference/pcie.c).

Signed-off-by: OpenWiFi BCM4360 Project <bcm4360@localhost>
---
 1 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
diff --git a/brcmfmac/pcie.c b/brcmfmac/pcie.c
index 9a0bdc8..c4a4faf 100644
--- a/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -748,9 +1044,11 @@ static int brcmf_pcie_exit_download_state(struct brcmf_pciedev_info *devinfo,
 {
 	struct brcmf_core *core;
 
-	if (devinfo->ci->chip == BRCM_CC_43602_CHIP_ID) {
+	if (devinfo->ci->chip == BRCM_CC_4360_CHIP_ID ||
+	    devinfo->ci->chip == BRCM_CC_43602_CHIP_ID) {
 		core = brcmf_chip_get_core(devinfo->ci, BCMA_CORE_INTERNAL_MEM);
-		brcmf_chip_resetcore(core, 0, 0, 0);
+		if (core)
+			brcmf_chip_resetcore(core, 0, 0, 0);
 	}
 
 	if (!brcmf_chip_set_active(devinfo->ci, resetintr))
--
2.39.2
